(*
expect:
true
true
true
true
true
true
*)
(* rete#190 sub-project A: C-heap accounting invariants. Absolute values vary
   run-to-run, so this asserts only what holds on every run and on BOTH paths
   (A solidified image, B .oimg): the high-water strictly exceeds what is
   currently outstanding, frees never exceed allocs (and at least one has
   happened), a failure count is a non-negative number, and something has in
   fact been allocated by the time an image is running. Exercises prim 152 ->
   the CHeapStats class end-to-end.
   NOTE: this is the C heap, NOT the GC arena that 01_invariants covers. The
   two being confused is what let a leak run for a week unseen.
   `1 asString` below is a deliberate warm-up allocation. None of the seam's
   six call sites (dispatch.c printString-on-genuine-Symbol/asString,
   platform.c asSymbol, vm.c bind:to:/instructionAt:put:, gc.c float_alloc's
   slab growth) fire during VM boot or from printing plain booleans, so
   without it `allocs` stays 0 and `allocs > 0` below would be vacuously
   false rather than actually exercised.
   `#foo printString` is a SECOND, load-bearing warm-up: it is the only path
   in the VM that calls oevm_free (dispatch.c:1635, the genuine-Symbol '#'
   prefix build — booleans take the early-return branch just above it and
   never reach the malloc). Without an alloc-THEN-free, out_bytes only ever
   rises, so out_high == out_bytes exactly at read time and `outHigh >
   outBytes` — or even `>=` — cannot distinguish a correct field order from
   outBytes/outHigh transposed in platform.c's prim arm or setFromList:. Do
   NOT simplify this away: the freed temp buffer is what makes outHigh
   strictly exceed the outBytes left standing by the still-outstanding
   `asString` allocation, and it is what makes `frees > 0` observable at
   all. *)
class CHeapInvariantsTest packageUsing: manifest = () (
public main: platform args: args = (
  | s |
  1 asString.
  #foo printString.
  s:: platform cheapStats.
  (s outHigh > s outBytes) printString println.
  (s allocs >= s frees) printString println.
  (s frees > 0) printString println.
  (s fails >= 0) printString println.
  (s allocs > 0) printString println.
  (s outBytes >= 0) printString println.
)
) : (
)
